WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:00.953
- All right, y'all.

00:00:00.953 --> 00:00:02.150
I always like to close out the show

00:00:02.150 --> 00:00:03.620
with something cool that will hopefully

00:00:03.620 --> 00:00:04.840
leave all of us feeling happy.

00:00:04.840 --> 00:00:06.040
This is What I'm Liking.

00:00:08.328 --> 00:00:09.550
(audience clapping)

00:00:09.550 --> 00:00:13.470
There are so many mysteries in
this ever expanding universe.

00:00:13.470 --> 00:00:14.960
Like, have you ever thought about

00:00:14.960 --> 00:00:17.160
what's going on miles
below the ocean surface?

00:00:17.160 --> 00:00:20.070
The bizarre creatures, plant
life that actually survives.

00:00:20.070 --> 00:00:21.340
I watch these shows all the time.

00:00:21.340 --> 00:00:22.290
I'm obsessed.

00:00:22.290 --> 00:00:23.620
One of my favorite aquariums,

00:00:23.620 --> 00:00:26.590
the Monterey aquarium here in
California has a new exhibit,

00:00:26.590 --> 00:00:28.260
that's giving people an up close

00:00:28.260 --> 00:00:31.560
and personal glimpse of what
happens deep down in the sea.

00:00:31.560 --> 00:00:32.530
It's super cool.

00:00:32.530 --> 00:00:34.070
And I wanted them to tell us all about it.

00:00:34.070 --> 00:00:37.010
So we have the director of
interpretive programs, Natalia

00:00:37.010 --> 00:00:38.270
on the line right now.

00:00:38.270 --> 00:00:40.320
She watches on KSBW eight.

00:00:40.320 --> 00:00:41.393
What's up.

00:00:42.500 --> 00:00:43.486
- Hi, Kelly.

00:00:43.486 --> 00:00:45.020
How are you?

00:00:45.020 --> 00:00:46.470
- Hello.

00:00:46.470 --> 00:00:48.040
Oh, I've actually been
where you're kinda standing.

00:00:48.040 --> 00:00:48.873
I love that.

00:00:48.873 --> 00:00:49.706
So it's great to meet you.

00:00:49.706 --> 00:00:51.500
I'm totally geeking
out about this exhibit.

00:00:51.500 --> 00:00:53.200
I cannot wait to come back.

00:00:53.200 --> 00:00:55.720
So putting this exhibition on,

00:00:55.720 --> 00:00:56.970
this has been kind of crazy, right?

00:00:56.970 --> 00:00:59.370
It's been quite the feat, right?

00:00:59.370 --> 00:01:01.860
- Yes. I mean that doesn't even cover it.

00:01:01.860 --> 00:01:05.040
We have had R and D years in the making

00:01:05.040 --> 00:01:08.590
to open up into the deep
our undiscovered oceans.

00:01:08.590 --> 00:01:10.450
Guests that come get to go

00:01:10.450 --> 00:01:12.690
as if they're diving down themselves.

00:01:12.690 --> 00:01:14.690
They start here in front of the open sea

00:01:14.690 --> 00:01:16.460
and then they take a deep dive,

00:01:16.460 --> 00:01:18.970
where they could see over
50 different species.

00:01:18.970 --> 00:01:21.270
We have our bloody belly comb jelly,

00:01:21.270 --> 00:01:23.130
say that five times fast.

00:01:23.130 --> 00:01:24.390
But the coolest thing is that

00:01:24.390 --> 00:01:26.580
some of these animals
have never been exhibited,

00:01:26.580 --> 00:01:28.740
and this exhibit will
have quite a long run.

00:01:28.740 --> 00:01:30.620
So you might come back
in a couple of years

00:01:30.620 --> 00:01:32.320
and see totally different animals.

00:01:32.320 --> 00:01:34.330
It's really, really exciting.

00:01:34.330 --> 00:01:35.200
- That's so cool.

00:01:35.200 --> 00:01:37.230
And it looks like they
just, it looks futuristic.

00:01:37.230 --> 00:01:38.290
It's all like (Kelly beeps).

00:01:38.290 --> 00:01:39.224
All the color, it's so cool.

00:01:39.224 --> 00:01:40.820
Was, I'm like a child.

00:01:40.820 --> 00:01:42.910
I'm like 40 years old
and I'm a child still.

00:01:42.910 --> 00:01:44.910
Was it tough to put the exhibit together?

00:01:44.910 --> 00:01:46.570
'Cause you're trying to like,

00:01:46.570 --> 00:01:50.700
remake what's happening
miles down the ocean, so.

00:01:50.700 --> 00:01:53.370
- Yeah. And you know, one
of the original visions

00:01:53.370 --> 00:01:56.380
of one of our founders, David
Packard, was what would happen

00:01:56.380 --> 00:01:59.140
if you put engineers
and scientists together?

00:01:59.140 --> 00:02:01.410
You get into the deep,
you get this exhibit

00:02:01.410 --> 00:02:04.450
because the engineers
use their engineering

00:02:04.450 --> 00:02:07.790
to put together things like
remotely operated vehicles,

00:02:07.790 --> 00:02:09.700
where we could actually travel down deep

00:02:09.700 --> 00:02:11.310
where humans can't go.

00:02:11.310 --> 00:02:13.940
And collect these animals in
the way that doesn't harm them.

00:02:13.940 --> 00:02:15.870
And then our scientists come in,

00:02:15.870 --> 00:02:19.300
and they figure out exactly
just the right pH of the water,

00:02:19.300 --> 00:02:20.410
how cold it needs to be,

00:02:20.410 --> 00:02:22.240
and all of the animal care side

00:02:22.240 --> 00:02:23.780
to actually exhibit these animals,

00:02:23.780 --> 00:02:25.660
so you and I could see them.

00:02:25.660 --> 00:02:27.120
- It is so cool.

00:02:27.120 --> 00:02:28.610
Thank you so much, Natalia.

00:02:28.610 --> 00:02:30.540
I cannot wait to come back and see y'all.

00:02:30.540 --> 00:02:31.690
I'm so stoked about it.

00:02:31.690 --> 00:02:34.169
I'm liking your post right now, okay?

00:02:34.169 --> 00:02:35.002
(audience clapping)

00:02:35.002 --> 00:02:35.840
- Yay. Thank you.

00:02:35.840 --> 00:02:37.270
Please. Come back.

00:02:37.270 --> 00:02:38.380
- All right, well that's not all.

00:02:38.380 --> 00:02:40.970
Our season long partner
Pilot Pen makers of G2,

00:02:40.970 --> 00:02:42.630
the go-to pen of the Kelly Clarkson show

00:02:42.630 --> 00:02:44.480
want to honor ultimate over achievers.

00:02:44.480 --> 00:02:47.190
I would definitely say
that's your entire team

00:02:47.190 --> 00:02:48.810
at the Monterey aquarium.

00:02:48.810 --> 00:02:50.290
So they're gonna be writing
the aquarium a check

00:02:50.290 --> 00:02:52.204
for a thousand dollars.

00:02:52.204 --> 00:02:53.412
(audience cheering)

00:02:53.412 --> 00:02:54.637
- Thank you, Kelly.

00:02:54.637 --> 00:02:56.547
Thank you so so much.

00:02:56.547 --> 00:02:58.397
- [Kelly] Thank you so much, Natalia.

